      "text": "Starting with the given product $(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)$, we apply the distributive property to expand it:\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2(7 - 2x) - 5x(7 - 2x) + 4(7 - 2x)\n\\]\n\nExpanding each term,\n\n\\begin{align*}\n3x^2(7 - 2x) &= 21x^2 - 6x^3 \\\\\n-5x(7 - 2x) &= -35x + 10x^2 \\\\\n4(7 - 2x) &= 28 - 8x\n\\end{align*}\n\nCombining these results, we get:\n\n\\[\n21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x = -6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28 = -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nThus, the coefficients are $a = -6$, $b = 31$, $c = -43$, and $d = 28$. To find $8a + 4b + 2c + d$, we substitute these values:\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term,\n\n\\begin{align*}\n8(-6) &= -48 \\\\\n4(31) &= 124 \\\\\n2(-43) &= -86 \\\\\n28 &= 28\n\\end{align*}\n\nSumming these values,\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28 = 28\n\\]\n\nTherefore, $8a + 4b + 2c + d = \\boxed{28}$.",
