      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by expanding the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\). We use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials) to do this.\n\nFirst, we distribute each term in the first polynomial to each term in the second polynomial:\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) + (-5x) \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the multiplications:\n\n\\[\n= 21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine like terms:\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nSo, the expanded form of the product is:\n\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nFrom this, we can identify the coefficients \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\na = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43, \\quad d = 28\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the arithmetic operations step by step:\n\n\\[\n= -48 + 124 - 86 + 28\n\\]\n\\[\n= (-48 + 124) + (-86 + 28)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 76 - 58\n\\]\n\\[\n= 18\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
