      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) and find the values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\), we will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials).\n\nFirst, we distribute each term in the first polynomial to each term in the second polynomial:\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) + (-5x) \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform each multiplication:\n\n\\[\n= 21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine like terms:\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nWe have the polynomial in the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), where:\n\\[\na = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43, \\quad d = 28\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate each term:\n\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48\n\\]\n\\[\n4(31) = 124\n\\]\n\\[\n2(-43) = -86\n\\]\n\\[\n28 = 28\n\\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28\n\\]\n\nFirst, add \\(-48\\) and \\(124\\):\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 = 76\n\\]\n\nNext, add \\(-86\\):\n\n\\[\n76 - 86 = -10\n\\]\n\nFinally, add \\(28\\):\n\n\\[\n-10 + 28 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\) is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
